g.\n\n10.**Round, red things are not white.**.\n    - This means that if something is round and red, it is not white.\n\n11.**All nice, white things are not red.**.\n    - This means that if something is nice, white, it is not red.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Harry is big.".\n\n- From point 8, we know that if Harry is rough, it must not be round.\n- From point 9, we know that if Harry is round, it must not be nice.\n- From point 10, we know that if Harry is nice, it must not be big.\n- From point 11, we know that if Harry is nice and white, it must not be red.\n\nSince Harry is nice and rough (from points 6 and 8), he must not be round (from point 8).Therefore, Harry must not be big (from point 9).\n\nThus, the statement "Harry is big" is false based on the given information.\n\n# Answer:.\nB) False.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
